SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,reading
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nJoin the Humboldt Park Branch for a screen
 ing of Inventing Improv! It may be Chicago’s greatest cultural export: i
 mprovised theater that was carried out into the world by the likes of Bill
  Murray\, Tina Fey\, Amy Poehler\, and Stephen Colbert. But this art form 
 wasn’t created by a funny man - it was devised by a woman who wasn’t o
 ut for laughs. Explore the life and legacy of Viola Spolin\, the social-wo
 rker-turned-theater guru known as The Mother of Improv. Feel free to bring
  your favorite snack to \\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.c
 om/events/6a05f073177319280019b4b7
LOCATION:Humboldt Park\, 1605 N. Troy St.\, Chicago\, IL 60647
URL:https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/events/6a05f073177319280019b4b7
